A||||5||extinct||rebuilt unloaded calipers?||||1||
Z||000000||extinct||12-11-2001||02:12 AM||||When you purchase a rebuilt unloaded caliper for an 88 does it normally come with attaching bolts (t-55)  and the rubber seals that go around the attaching bolts?<P>Or do you have to buy a "loaded" caliper to get new attaching bolts (t-55) and seals?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||GTDude||12-12-2001||12:03 PM||||Normally you will not get new bolts either way.  They have to be purchased separately, but most parts stores can get them.<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||3
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||12-12-2001||02:40 PM||||No to both ?'s||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||12-12-2001||10:04 PM||||I just purchased a loaded caliper from Checker for $107.99. They said they will beat any price. I told them <A HREF="http://www.partsamerica.com" TARGET=_blank>www.partsamerica.com</A>  has them listed for 107.99, they matched it! Raybestos too.<P>Now, the caliper did <B>NOT</B> come with any mounting bolts! It also didn't come with any of the parking brake hardware (a bracket for the cable and the lever).<P>It did come with new sliders and boots. New pad sliders too.<P>Not sure what you mean by, "...the rubber seals that go around the attaching bolts...", but I think you mean the boots for the sliders (the attaching bolts go through these). Those are included.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||extinct||12-13-2001||12:37 AM||||scca, thank you!  Thats the exact info I needed.  Since the loaded caliper came with new raybestos pads, you must have replaced both rear calipers?||||reg||1
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||12-13-2001||11:24 PM||||I was changing my pads when I ended up making the piston come all the way out. This caliper has seen better days, so I just replaced it... replaced the pads in the other caliper too.||||reg||1
